menu "sys_data_connector"

    config SYS_DATA_CONNECTOR_MAX
        int "Connectors"
        default 16
        range 5 32
        help
          Registry slots: the 5 system connectors (logs, errors, telemetry,
          events, all events), the user connectors and the mirrors (sys_remote
          makes two per board that has a remote device).

    config SYS_DATA_CONNECTOR_BINDINGS
        int "Bindings per connector"
        default 3
        range 1 8

    config SYS_DATA_CONNECTOR_SUBSCRIBERS
        int "Subscribers per connector"
        default 4
        range 1 8
        help
          Peers subscribed to one connector (SUBSCRIBE): the app, a test host.

    config SYS_DATA_CONNECTOR_BUF_POOL
        int "Receive buffers (bytes)"
        default 2048
        range 0 16384
        help
          The buffers of every connector that keeps what comes in (LATEST: one
          message, FIFO: a ring), taken at create from one static pool and
          given back at remove. A create that does not fit: ERR_CONN_POOL_FULL.

    config SYS_DATA_CONNECTOR_QUEUE_SIZE
        int "Queue (bytes)"
        default 4608
        range 1024 32768
        help
          Ring buffer of frames waiting for the connector task; each takes
          its length + ~12 bytes, and the frame being sent keeps its room
          until every target has it. A full queue drops sends. Multiple of 4.

    config SYS_DATA_CONNECTOR_TASK_PRIO
        int "Task priority"
        default 4
        range 1 24
        help
          Below the router tasks: streams wait, commands don't.

    config SYS_DATA_CONNECTOR_TASK_STACK
        int "Task stack (bytes)"
        default 4096
        range 2048 32768
        help
          Holds a whole stream frame (CMD_FRAME_MAX) while it goes to a
          subscriber.

endmenu
